# Workspace brain — Cursor

Portable multi-agent workspace. Contract: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). This rule is `alwaysApply:true`
so every model in Cursor inherits it.

**Always-on set on Cursor (harness-map #3):** `AGENTS.md` (via this rule + User Rules beacon) +
this file + `01-agent-controller.mdc`. Do **not** treat `CLAUDE.md` as Cursor standing law — it is
the Claude Code adapter (ritual format + slash skills). If Cursor injects it anyway, prefer
`AGENTS.md` + this rule on conflict.

## Side-chat inbox (every parent turn)

Before continuing substantive work in a **parent / main** thread: if
`06-context/side-chat-inbox.md` exists and frontmatter `status` is `pending`, read it first, fold
**For the parent** into the reply (or act on it), then set `status: consumed` or delete the file.
Written by `/handback` / [[side-chat-handback]] from a side chat — no copy/paste required. Not a
session-end. Skill: `03-skills/side-chat-handback/SKILL.md`.

## Session start

Before the first reply in a new session:

1. Root = directory containing `AGENTS.md`. Read: `AGENTS.md` → `03-skills/skills.registry.json` →
   `02-shared-references/trigger-routes.md` (curated head) → `06-context/` (role, **project-context
   stubs only** — not `project-context-detail.md` / `project-registry.md` unless the task needs them —
   session-log head, `memory/MEMORY.md`). Active project: read `SESSION-STATE.md` **Live handoff** first.
   Also run the side-chat inbox check above.
2. **Notices (optional, top of ritual):** if
   `07-projects/19-workspace-brain/reports/harness-map.stamp` exists and its `date:` is **>30 days**
   old, warn once: harness map stale → `/harness-map` when convenient (not a blocker). **Silent if
   the stamp is missing** (no nag before the first map). Same pattern as Claude's SessionStart Notices.
   If `skill-routing-harness.stamp` is missing or `python3 09-tools/evaluate-skill-routing.py --stale`
   fails, run the evaluator and surface FAIL (silent on pass). Not a daemon; also run after skill /
   trigger-routes / corpus edits, on a live mis-route (`--utterance`), and from `/health` + `/optimize`.
3. Emit the ritual:
```
[workspace: LOADED · {branch}@{short-sha} · {YYYY-MM-DD} · via:cursor-rule]
**✓ Workspace loaded** — {Machine} · {YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM}
- **Surface:** Cursor · **Model:** {model}
- **Last session:** {date} — {one-line}
- **Pending:** {N} → 06-context/project-context.md
- **Active:** {project} — {Live handoff one-liner}
What's on the agenda?
```
Machines: `Voyager-2.local`→Personal MBP · `CS-K746DRWXY1`/`CS-KQ23N94M0W`/`seansands.local`→Work MBP ·
`Enterprise`→Windows.

## Model swap / resume

Re-anchor: re-read Live handoff + load skills (`trigger-routes` / registry `load_chains`) before acting.
Update Live handoff on meaningful change (`Cursor · {model}`).

## Parallel Task agents

Prefer `.cursor/agents/*`. Workers skip the ritual. Parent owns Live handoff; workers write
`06-context/sessions/` fragments only — never race-append `session-log.md`.

## Writes

Any model may write behind the gates in `01-agent-controller.mdc` / AGENTS.md. Never run the retired
`compile-cursor-rules.py` (archived — it would overwrite AGENTS.md).

## Skills & conventions

Route skills; don't bulk-load. Artifacts: `context_descriptor_vN.N_YYYY-MM-DD.ext`. `[[wikilinks]]`.
Archive don't delete. Never rename `SKILL.md` (use `aliases`). Never hand-edit generated files
(`skills.registry.json`, `trigger-routes.md`).
